AC+B&=\sqrt{91}+10\\
CD&=\sqrt{7}\\
EF&=\sqrt{91}\\
EB&=10-3=7.
\end{align*}Therefore, the area of $ADC$ equals \[\frac{1}{2}(7+\sqrt{91})(\sqrt{91}+10)=\frac{1}{2}(7\sqrt{91}+10\sqrt{91}+70)=\frac{1}{2}[9\sqrt{91}+70]=\frac{227}{a} + \frac{9\sqrt{91}}{2a}= \boxed{\frac{227+9\sqrt{91}}{2a}}.\] </think> <answer separately </answer>
